## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement a simple, reliable streaming ingest with validation, a practical approach to schema evolution, and basic operations like dead-lettering, archiving, rollback, and monitoring at beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub as a source and dead-lettering for bad messages
- Dataflow (Beam) for parsing/validation
- BigQuery core schema + extras JSON field for evolution
- Idempotent writes using insertId or MERGE
- Rollback strategies using Pub/Sub replay or GCS archive
- Basic monitoring and alerts for data quality

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-beam style pseudocode
// Read from Pub/Sub, parse JSON, validate required fields, emit rows to BigQuery
class ParseAndValidateDoFn extends DoFn {
  processElement(ctx) {
    const msg = JSON.parse(ctx.element);
    if (!msg.timestamp || !msg.user_id || !msg.endpoint) return;
    const row = {core_field1: msg.timestamp, core_field2: msg.user_id, core_field3: msg.endpoint, extras: JSON.stringify(msg.extras || {})};
    yield row;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test schema-evolution choices and measure their impact on query performance?
- What would you monitor to detect data quality regressions in this pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of data privacy, per-tenant isolation, and practical use of GCP data tools in a beginner-friendly setup.

## Key Concepts

- Data masking in streaming + Data Catalog lineage
- Per-tenant isolation with BigQuery datasets
- Rollback using backup tables and views
- Schema drift handling and late data tolerance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-Dataflow DoFn masking PII
class MaskPiIFn extends DoFn {
  processElement(ctx) {
    const record = ctx.element;
    record.email = mask(record.email);
    record.phone = mask(record.phone);
    return record;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test data contracts in Data Catalog?
- How would you scale this pattern to 10s of tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses design for multi-tenant data observability, lineage, and controlled evolution. Focus on practical patterns and failure handling beyond basic ingestion.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation and schema evolution
- Exactly-once processing and idempotency
- End-to-end lineage with Data Catalog
- Rollback by time travel + Pub/Sub replay
- Cost and fault-tolerance considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: derive per-tenant lineage and offset tracking for replay
function processEvent(evt, tenant) {
  // ensure idempotent write
  const key = `${tenant}:${evt.id}`;
  if (store.has(key)) return;
  writeToBQ(tenant, evt);
  store.set(key, true);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback across tenants with partial data loss?
- How would you monitor data freshness and SLA adherence per tenant?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests end-to-end real-time data engineering competencies on GCP, including multi-tenant isolation, dynamic schema evolution, data contracts, and rollback semantics, plus cross-cloud replication and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow templates
- Per-tenant isolation using partitioned BigQuery datasets
- Central schema registry in Data Catalog for dynamic evolution
- End-to-end lineage and data contracts
- 24-hour per-tenant rollback via BigQuery time travel
- Cross-region replication to Snowflake via Snowpipe

## Code Example

```java
// Dataflow pipeline with tenant isolation and schema validation
public class TenantPipeline {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PipelineOptions options = PipelineOptionsFactory.fromArgs(args).create();
        Pipeline pipeline = Pipeline.create(options);

        pipeline
            .apply("Read from Pub/Sub", PubsubIO.readMessagesWithAttributes()
                .fromSubscription(options.getSubscription()))
            .apply("Extract tenant ID", ParDo.of(new ExtractTenantDoFn()))
            .apply("Validate against schema", ParDo.of(new SchemaValidationDoFn()))
            .apply("Write to tenant BigQuery", new TenantBigQueryWrite());

        pipeline.run();
    }
}
```
